Let \(M\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}\). Then \(M\) is column sufficient if and only if, for every pair of disjoint index sets \(\alpha,\beta\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}\) with \(\alpha\cup\beta\neq\varnothing\), there is no vector \(\begin{bmatrix}x_\alpha\\x_\beta\end{bmatrix}>0\) satisfying
\[
0\neq
\begin{bmatrix}
M_{\alpha\alpha}&-M_{\alpha\beta}\\
-M_{\beta\alpha}&M_{\beta\beta}
\end{bmatrix}
\begin{bmatrix}x_\alpha\\x_\beta\end{bmatrix}
\leq 0,
\]
where the inequalities are componentwise.

